# rl_propulsion.kfl - a craft that pays for its thrust.
#
# The smallest programme that exercises the propulsion model end to
# end: a craft in low orbit whose assembly holds propellant, a main
# engine and a vernier at different specific impulses, and the four
# published components of a propulsion observe read back in the
# reward and in the termination predicate.
#
# The reward is a stand-in and not a task. It pays for velocity change
# still affordable and charges for propellant spent, which is what a
# programme conditioning on this form would read; the episode ends
# when the tank runs dry, which is a state the model can reach and a
# controller has to be able to see coming.

form RL_PROPULSION

fn world w
    astro_body earth gm=3.986004418e14 mass=5.972e24

    astro_body craft assembly="../examples/assets/propellant_box.k26asm" parent=earth pos_x=7.0e6 pos_y=0.0 pos_z=0.0 vel_x=0.0 vel_y=7546.0 vel_z=0.0 quat_w=1.0 quat_x=0.0 quat_y=0.0 quat_z=0.0 omega_x=0.0 omega_y=0.0 omega_z=0.0

    episode
        control_dt 1.0
        horizon 64
        substeps 8
        terminated when fuel_propellant_fraction < 0.001
    end

    action burn box 0.0 1.0 default 0.0
    action steer box -1.0 1.0 default 0.0

    on_step
        craft.main.throttle = burn
        craft.vernier.throttle = steer * steer
    end

    observe propulsion of craft as fuel
    observe attitude of craft as att
    observe craft from earth mode=geometric as trk

    objective
        reward fuel_delta_v_remaining * 0.001 - burn * 0.01
    end
end

end
